  :refs ["futon2/holes/labs/wm-contract/PROOF-2a-THEOREM-draft-2026-09-24.md" "futon3c/holes/labs/M-futon-seams/proto/instance-5.edn#10501d40" "futon3/library/software-design/adapter-pattern.flexiarg"]
  :body "Clause 0, construction (W0, X0(d)) and the carrier. (1) No pattern produces the want :impersonation-retired, so p(all wants) is 0 under every kernel at every horizon. The pattern that would produce it, software-design/adapter-pattern, exists but declares @arg rather than @flexiarg, so it cannot be cited (28 library files do this). The refusal is caused by a header defect in the library, not by missing knowledge; a typed :unproduced-need finding should say which. (2) The carrier: 7 of 21 pattern pairs have no meet, so this structure fails CascadeOrder.hasMeets, which PROOF-2a's W0 requires. With two roots (count-every-card-back, choose-the-grain-where-state-lives) and no common context above them, the cascade is a forest of two trees joined lower down, not a semilattice with meets."}
